Use identities:

- \(\csc\theta=\frac{1}{\sin\theta}\), so \(\frac{\csc\theta}{\sin\theta}=\frac{1}{\sin^2\theta}\)
- \(\cot\theta=\frac{\cos\theta}{\sin\theta}\) and \(\tan\theta=\frac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}\), so
  \[
  \frac{\cot\theta}{\tan\theta}
  =\frac{\cos\theta/\sin\theta}{\sin\theta/\cos\theta}
  =\frac{\cos^2\theta}{\sin^2\theta}
  \]

Thus,
\[
\frac{1}{\sin^2\theta}-\frac{\cos^2\theta}{\sin^2\theta}
=\frac{1-\cos^2\theta}{\sin^2\theta}
=\frac{\sin^2\theta}{\sin^2\theta}
=1
\]

